sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) self-organized magnetic-drop phyllotaxis & imperfect pitchfork cascade — MorphoEval overall 91.0/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py` (91.2/100, up from 55.6/100 in Pass 1; +35.6 overall). The remediated v2 script implements both linear silicone-oil dish advection r_k = R_0*(1 + k*G) and exponential shoot apical meristem advection r_k = R_0*exp(k*G), solves the exact 2-drop and full-chain Hessian fold (G_fold = 0.773484 exp, 2.514560 lin) and dynamical pitchfork (G_c1 = 0.860537 exp, 3.631432 lin) thresholds with exact parity to the 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_031_magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis.lean` (C(4,7)=+27687, C(3,5)=-6144), traces the full regular-spiral equilibrium locus F(G, dphi) = 0 across both the Fibonacci cascade (r = 0.99999, RMSE = 0.065 deg across 10 benchmark G points; Delaunay pair (5, 8) at G=0.06) and the disconnected Lucas branch (1,3)->(3,4)->(4,7)->(7,11) (RMSE = 0.141 deg; Delaunay pair (4, 7) at G=0.11), runs repulsive power-law universality sweeps (gamma in {1, 3, 5}), single-drop memory ablation (N_mem = 1 -> 180.0 deg), and Voronoi packing regularity KS tests (CV = 0.132 vs random CV = 0.612, p < 1e-8), and segments N = 123 woody scale umbos on `conifer_cone_specimen.jpg` with log-polar 2D FFT extraction confirming opposing (5, 8) Fibonacci parastichies. Overall 91.0/100 (faithfulness 90.4, reproducibility 92.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_comparison.png: rendered output of 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 1299361 B, 2590×1820 px, artifact_sha256 779d9de0700bbef59454bf311549f619c754aa2ee9d124d3e314546ea02b7e79 (sha256 779d9de0700bbef59454bf311549f619c754aa2ee9d124d3e314546ea02b7e79), spec_fingerprint 33eddc6c7f7154d2ce87a1a999bc4ec67c98aaa43e0d2412fb26a2fc20bc5041. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 33eddc6c7f7154d2ce87a1a999bc4ec67c98aaa43e0d2412fb26a2fc20bc5041; artifact_sha256: 779d9de0700bbef59454bf311549f619c754aa2ee9d124d3e314546ea02b7e79; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/conifer_cone_specimen.jpg=7bcb68e856d4db53..., datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_reference.json=9ae33106a0fea23f..., datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/paper_citations.bib=2c3aa1ec0e4c53de...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Douady & Couder (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098-2101 iterative magnetic-dipole repulsion energy E(phi) = sum_{k>=1} d_k(phi, phi_{n-k})^{-3} on a circular rim r = R_0 controlled by dimensionless plastochron ratio G = V * T / R_0 | Douady & Couder (1992) Fig. 3 & (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 178:255-274 supercritical (1,1)->(1,2) pitchfork bifurcation and imperfect pitchfork cascade along the Fibonacci branch (1,2,3,5,8,13) -> 137.508 deg and disconnected Lucas branch (1,3,4,7,11) -> 99.502 deg; reconstructed_in_script: Exact 2-drop and full-chain Hessian fold (G_fold = 0.773484 exp / 2.514560 lin) and dynamical pitchfork (G_c1 = 0.860537 exp / 3.631432 lin) roots, regular-spiral zero-force equilibrium locus F(G, dphi) = 0, and adiabatic continuation along both Fibonacci (r = 0.99999, RMSE = 0.065 deg) and Lucas (RMSE = 0.141 deg) branches | Difference-of-Gaussians (DoG) scale-umbo segmentation (N = 123 scales) and log-polar (u = ln r, theta) 2D FFT spiral spectrum extraction confirming opposing (m_CW, m_CCW) = (5, 8) Fibonacci parastichies on `conifer_cone_specimen.jpg`; transfer_boundary: 2D planar/conical projection of radial meristem advection r_k = R_0 * exp(k*G) and silicone-oil ferrofluid dish advection r_k = R_0 * (1 + k*G) mapped onto apical conifer cone scale lattices; does_not_claim: Subcellular PIN1 polar auxin efflux carrier trafficking or continuous reaction-diffusion PDE dynamics on the meristem (covered in Slot 033 Jönsson et al. 2006 / Smith et al. 2006)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.91"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

